pkg:Evidence_v1_11_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.11.0 (MINOR release, kick-off recorded)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: user correctly caught that Iteration1's iterationStart/iterationEnd were fabricated -- an invented 2-week window with no basis, the same G31 mistake already caught once this session, just relocated. Checked first whether those dates were ever required: read the SHACL clauses directly, both conditional (fire only if present and inconsistent), so nothing required them -- removed. Read the standard's real answer for dependency/priority planning without calendar fabrication: Roadmap + RoadmapHorizon (Now/Next/Later, closed 3-member enum), quoting the standard's own reasoning -- 'chosen over date-pinned columns because horizon bands carry honest uncertainty, whereas dates on unstarted work carry false precision.' Built one Roadmap and assigned all 5 Stories a horizon and rank purely from the dependency graph: STORY-1 Now/1, STORY-2 Next/2, STORY-3/4/5 Later/3-5 -- no dates anywhere in this structure. Also corrected a stale-date accuracy issue found in passing: plannedAt and all 5 CostEstimate estimatedAt fields had carried over 2026-08-31 from earlier in the session; corrected to the actual current date, 2026-09-01. Recorded KickOff per the user's explicit direction once the roadmap was ready: KickOff_Declared, decidedBy Owner, kickedOffAt the real current moment -- genuinely when planning concluded and the first item went live, not backfilled. Re-verified: pipeline order unaffected (Roadmap/RoadmapHorizon/KickOff are not pipeline-tracked types), full SHACL 0 violations."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "1c20241f87fdd4e2e334338908cb03059c208b07525ee50581dfbb000cf86f2d"^^xsd:string .
